scenario: overflow_places
A key that has been used from 1,000 clients keeps no more places of that kind: the next client is counted in the overflow row, which is not a place and never raises. A new country on the same request still does.

step 1  0s       app     request  198.51.100.7 US AS64500 app-{i}/1 x1000
  nothing raised

step 2  8d       app     request  198.51.100.7 US AS64500 late/1
  nothing raised

step 3  8d1m     app     request  198.51.100.7 DE AS64500 late/2
  detection #1 incident 1: new_country high
      observed new country DE
      baseline US (1001 requests)
      from     198.51.100.7
      network  198.51.100.0/24
      country  DE
      as       AS64500 Example Net
      client   late/2
  alert: incident 1 opened, high, rules [new_country], about new_country

incidents at the end:
  #1 app open high rules [new_country], 1 detections, opened 192h1m0s, last fired 192h1m0s
